      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Joe Lee Griffin opened the Eagle Point Golf Club in 1990 on 144 acres at the foot of Oak Mountain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_point_alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2016, the Shelby County Planning Commission rezoned the former golf course into Griffin Park at Eagle Point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_point_alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Eagle Point lies at the foot of Double Oak Mountain, a rural area that stayed farmland until the late 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_point_alabama",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Developer John Reamer bought land around the golf course and built the Eagle Point subdivision, matching the course’s name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/eagle_point_alabama",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Early settlers from South Carolina, Tennessee, and Kentucky cleared land for crops and livestock in northern Shelby County, shaping the rural character that later became Eagle Point.",
